    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d695">

                <pb facs="0793" n="783" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg783"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">151.10/1970½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Assistant Secretary
                        of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-10-06">October 6, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I talked to Speaker Ray burn this morning on the subject of the Chinese
                    immigration bill. He said that it would be up before the Immigration Committee
                    this morning; that it was in good shape before the Committee but that there
                    would be some opposition to it on the floor; that they could easily get a rule
                    out of the Rules Committee; and that he thought it was in good shape, that there
                    would be some opposition to it, and that a letter from the Secretary of State to
                    be used on the floor would be very helpful.</p>
                <p>I told him that I thought I could assure him that there would be such a letter at
                    the appropriate time and that I would keep in touch with him in regard to
                    it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>B[<hi rendition="#small-caps">reckinridge</hi>] L[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ong</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
